sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant Order as OrderService
    participant Allocation as RealTimeAllocationService
    participant Store as RealTimeAllocationStore
    participant DB as PostgreSQL Database
    participant Engine as AllocationEngine
    participant Pricing as AllocationPricingService

    %% ==========================================
    %% 1. START REAL-TIME ALLOCATION
    %% ==========================================

    Note over Order,Allocation: Triggered automatically after a valid SalesOrder is created

    Order->>+Allocation: AllocateAsync(orderId)

    Allocation->>+Store: LoadForUpdateAsync(orderId)

    Store->>+DB: SELECT order lines, Retailer and MLOR
    Note right of DB: Include warehouse locations, batches<br/>and available inventory balances

    DB-->>Store: Order and inventory context
    deactivate DB

    Store-->>Allocation: RealTimeAllocationContext
    deactivate Store

    %% ==========================================
    %% 2. PREPARE CANDIDATES AND RECEIPT ETA
    %% ==========================================

    Note over Allocation,Engine: Evaluate eligible batches across multiple warehouses

    loop For each SalesOrderLine

        Allocation->>+Allocation: DistanceMeters(warehouse, retailer)

        Allocation-->>Allocation: Distance for each candidate
        deactivate Allocation

        Note over Allocation,Engine: Determine estimated receipt time using available<br/>distance and delivery assumptions

        Note over Allocation,Engine: Remaining shelf life at receipt =<br/>Expiration Time - Estimated Arrival Time

        %% ==========================================
        %% 3. FILTER AND SCORE BATCHES
        %% ==========================================

        Allocation->>+Engine: Allocate(lineRequest, batchCandidates)

        Note right of Engine: Apply hard eligibility filters:<br/>SKU, usable stock, expiry,<br/>service radius, ETA and MLOR

        Note right of Engine: Score eligible batches using<br/>remaining life, distance and<br/>quantity coverage weights

        Engine-->>Allocation: Selected fragments and exclusion reasons
        deactivate Engine

    end

    %% ==========================================
    %% 4. CHECK COMPLETE ORDER FULFILLMENT
    %% ==========================================

    alt All order lines can be fully allocated

        %% ==========================================
        %% 5. CALCULATE FINAL BATCH PRICES
        %% ==========================================

        Allocation->>+Pricing: PriceAsync(allocatedBatchParts)

        Note right of Pricing: Apply selected quantity promotion,<br/>then shelf-life percentage discount

        Pricing-->>Allocation: Final prices for allocated batches
        deactivate Pricing

        %% ==========================================
        %% 6. PERSIST ALLOCATION RESULT
        %% ==========================================

        Allocation->>+Store: AddRun(), AddAllocation(), AddReservation()

        Note over Allocation,Store: Persist all allocations and reservations atomically

        Store->>+DB: Validate stock and commit reservations
        Note right of DB: INSERT allocations, reservations,<br/>inventory transactions and quotation

        DB-->>Store: Transaction committed
        deactivate DB

        Store-->>Allocation: Allocation and quotation saved
        deactivate Store

        Allocation-->>Order: Allocation successful - Final quotation ready

    else At least one order line cannot be fulfilled

        Note over Allocation,Engine: Discard tentative selections for this order

        Allocation->>+Store: AddHistory(), SaveChangesAsync()

        Store->>+DB: UPDATE order allocation status to Insufficient Stock
        DB-->>Store: Shortage status recorded
        deactivate DB

        Store-->>Allocation: Failure recorded
        deactivate Store

        Allocation-->>Order: Insufficient stock - No reservation created

    end

    deactivate Allocation

    Note over Order,DB: Reservation concurrency and commit details are expanded in Figure 3.6.3